MAJOR_VERSION=4
STANDARD_VERSION=2
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=14
DESCRIPTION<<VER_END
PRE 4.2.0: Wi-Fi scan home SSID + SSID-based join; WSL detection; FlinstonePowershell bridge; Codex security fixes

- platform detection (kernel/core/platform/fl_platform.c): runtime tag of
  FL_PLATFORM_WSL / FL_PLATFORM_LINUX / FL_PLATFORM_MACOS; checks /proc/version
  and WSL_DISTRO_NAME so WSL1 and WSL2 are both detected; result cached
- FlinstonePowershell (tools/FlinstonePowershell/FlinstonePowershell.cpp):
  C++ bridge program for the WSL ↔ Windows Wi-Fi path; commands:
  wifi-scan, wifi-join, wifi-leave, wifi-status, platform; Windows build
  (make flinstone-ps-windows, links -lwlanapi -lole32 -liphlpapi -lws2_32)
  uses native WlanAPI:
  WlanOpenHandle/WlanCloseHandle (RAII), WlanEnumInterfaces, WlanScan +
  Sleep(1500) + WlanGetNetworkBssList for scanning (raw BSS IE parsing for
  auth mode: RSN IE tag 0x30 with AKM 00:0F:AC:08=SAE→wpa3, else wpa2;
  vendor IE 0xDD OUI 00:50:F2:01=WPA1), centre-frequency-to-band/channel
  conversion (2.4/5/6 GHz), WlanSetProfile (WPA2-PSK or open WLANProfile
  XML built in memory) + WlanConnect for wifi-join, WlanDisconnect for
  wifi-leave, WlanQueryInterface(wlan_intf_opcode_current_connection) for
  wifi-status; Linux dev build (make flinstone-ps) uses hardcoded stubs
- wifi host backend (net_wifi_host_linux.c): on WSL, probe_host_backend_once()
  routes through FlinstonePowershell instead of wpa_cli/nmcli; FL_WIFI_HOST_FLINSTONE_PS
  backend kind; exe located via FL_NET_WIFI_FLINSTONE_PS env var or PATH search;
  tab-separated key=value scan output parsed into fl_net_wifi_scan_entry_t;
  connect/disconnect call wifi-join/wifi-leave subcommands; after a successful
  connect the backend immediately queries wifi-status to cache the real Windows
  Wi-Fi IP (ipv4=, prefix=, gateway= fields from GetAdaptersAddresses via
  iphlpapi); a separate read_any_nonlo_ipv4() scan of getifaddrs() picks the
  WSL2 eth0 IP (e.g. 172.28.x.x) and caches it in s_wsl_bind_ipv4 —
  fl_net_wifi_host_linux_ipv4() returns this WSL IP so fl_net_wifi_netdev_up_
  with_ipv4() registers a real bindable Linux address; server host <wsl-ip>:
  <port> now succeeds instead of failing with EADDRNOTAVAIL; the Windows
  adapter IP (s_fps_ipv4, e.g. 192.168.1.235) is exposed via the new
  fl_net_wifi_host_linux_windows_ipv4() API for display only; wifi status and
  wifi join now print a separate "Windows Wi-Fi IP: ..." line showing the
  router-assigned address; server host automatically calls
  fl_net_wifi_host_linux_server_proxy() which runs FlinstonePowershell server-
  proxy <wsl_ip> <port> — a new subcommand that adds a Windows netsh portproxy
  rule forwarding the Windows IP:<port> to WSL, enabling LAN-wide access
  (requires FlinstonePowershell.exe run as admin); server-proxy-del <port>
  removes the rule; cache is cleared on disconnect; MinGW cross-compile includes
  winsock2.h before iphlpapi.h so GetAdaptersAddresses and GAA types resolve
- wifi scan (lab backend): reads FL_NET_WIFI_HOME_SSID env var and includes the
  user's home network in scan results; FL_NET_WIFI_HOME_AUTH (open/wpa2/wpa3)
  and FL_NET_WIFI_HOME_BAND (2/5/6) are optional — defaults are wpa2 and 2.4 GHz
- wifi join: lab backend no longer requires the target SSID to appear in the last
  scan; if the network is absent a synthetic scan entry is built from the supplied
  SSID so home and hidden networks can be joined directly by name
- wifi join: password is now prompted interactively (no-echo) after the command is
  entered, similar to sudo; usage is `wifi join <ssid>` or `wifi join -b <bssid> <ssid>`
- wifi join: when the session carries sudo elevation, prompts "Sudo Password: " first
  to re-authenticate, then "WiFi Password: " — distinguishing the two credentials
- scripts/install_deps.sh: added wpasupplicant and network-manager as runtime deps
  for the Linux Wi-Fi host backend (wpa_cli / nmcli); mingw-w64 installed only on
  WSL (detected via /proc/version or WSL_DISTRO_NAME) since it is only needed for
  the FlinstonePowershell.exe Windows cross-compile path
- README.md: added sudo ./scripts/install_deps.sh instruction under Prerequisites
- security: shell-escape SSID and passphrase before popen nmcli/wpa_cli calls
  (shell injection via crafted SSID or passphrase — net_wifi_host_linux.c)
- security: reject sparse file-transfer chunks whose file_offset != bytes already
  received; also reject chunks that exceed the advertised file size
  (uninitialized-memory write to disk via out-of-order chunks — net_file_delivery.c)
- fix: preserve statted file_size across fl_server_file_offer_create memset so
  total_chunks is not always zero (cmd_server_file.c)
- fix: add missing braces in fl_net_sock_native_close so listener sockets do not
  close tcp_conn_id 0 or call stack_unlock without a matching lock (net_sock_native.c)
- server-bridge (FlinstonePowershell + net_wifi_host_linux.c): userspace TCP relay
  for LAN→WSL server access without Windows admin rights; FlinstonePowershell
  server-bridge <port> listens on 0.0.0.0:<port> (all Windows adapters including
  Wi-Fi) and forwards each accepted connection to 127.0.0.1:<port> via WSL2
  loopback forwarding — no netsh portproxy / no admin needed for ports >= 1024;
  implemented with two-thread-per-connection WinSock relay (relay_pair + relay_task,
  InterlockedDecrement ref counting for clean socket teardown); spawned in the
  background from Linux via fl_net_wifi_host_linux_server_bridge() using system()
  with &; verb_host() in cmd_server.c tries portproxy first then falls back to
  bridge so non-admin users get automatic LAN access
- tools/server_bridge.py: Python asyncio alternative to FlinstonePowershell
  server-bridge; same 0.0.0.0:<port>→127.0.0.1:<port> relay in ~70 lines;
  run with `python3 tools/server_bridge.py <port>` on Windows or via WSL interop
- Wi-Fi LAN server bridge: discover in-tree FlinstonePowershell.exe for WSL
  Wi-Fi scan/join, safely quote helper paths and credentials, refresh the
  router-assigned Windows Wi-Fi IP from wifi-status for server host hints,
  support server-bridge bind_ip/port/target_ip relays for WSL loopback or VM
  targets, add Python network_bridge.py target parity, and cover helper
  discovery plus bridge relay tests
- Raspberry Pi ARM build fix: net_file_delivery.h now directly declares the
  FILE_ACCEPT, FILE_DECLINE, and FILE_REVOKE encoder prototypes used by
  cmd_server_file.c, avoiding transitive contract-header assumptions on ARM
  compilers that treat implicit function declarations as fatal
VER_END
